  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedIncreaseOrDecreaseInAnnualRevenuesCausedByImportantRateChangesTextBlock id="HHE60759687E403C6B3DE58B8464A791E0" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&#xD;
		&lt;div&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;In anticipation of the Partnership&amp;#x2019;s obligation to file a Section 4 rate case no later than September 1, 2022, the Partnership entered into discussions with the RP16-301 and the RP19-445 interested parties (2022 Settlement Parties).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt; These discussions resulted in an agreement in principal resolving all rate case issues (2022 Settlement).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt; The 2022 Settlement was filed with the FERC and approved by order dated August 31, 2022, with new rates being placed into effect September 1, 2022.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt; Pursuant to the 2022 Settlement, there will be a rate moratorium wherein no new firm recourse rates can be placed into effect on the Partnership&amp;#x2019;s mainline or Eastchester facilities until September 1, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt; Following the conclusion of the moratorium, if no rate case is filed or if no new rate settlement is reached, the Partnership must file a section 4 rate case no later than September 1, 2027.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt; During the period of the moratorium, Iroquois reduced its rates in three step-downs as follows:&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;div style="text-align:center"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" style="margin-right:auto; margin-left:auto"&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;tr&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;td style="width:98.5pt; border-style:solid; border-width:1pt; padding-right:5.4pt; padding-left:5.4pt; vertical-align:top"&gt;&#xD;
							&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
								&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-weight:bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
							&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
							&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
