&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Brookfield, Connecticut Site Clean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Up&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 13.7pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On June 27, 2003, the Partnership purchased real property in Brookfield, Connecticut upon which it constructed its Brookfield compressor station (Brookfield Site or Site). On November 3, 2004, the Connecticut Department of Energy and Environmental Protection (DEEP) approved the Site&amp;#8217;s remediation plan and scope of work schedule. After the major clean-up, re-grading, and seeding work at the Brookfield Site was completed (with the exception of buried tires on the property which is discussed below), Iroquois received a Letter of No Audit (LNA) from the DEEP dated November 13, 2014.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The LNA states that the DEEP agrees with Iroquois&amp;#8217; Licensed Environmental Professional (LEP) that the site is now clean (with the exception of the buried tires on the property) and closes the Environmental Condition Assessment Form (ECAF) for the Brookfield Voluntary Cleanup.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;For the remaining buried tires on the Brookfield site, Iroquois has entered into the state Stewardship Program.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Stewardship Program requires monitoring of the tire area until 2041 and remediation of any erosion, subsidence, or tires that have worked their way to the surface. It is not anticipated that the ongoing monitoring of this site will have a material effect on the Partnership&amp;#8217;s financial condition or results of operations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 13.7pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Enhancement by Compression Project (ExC) &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;During 2019 the Partnership entered into precedent agreements with Con Edison and KeySpan Gas East Corporation d/b/a National Grid to develop and permit incremental pipeline delivery capacity to transport additional volumes of natural gas along Iroquois&amp;#8217; system to support design &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;day demand and the reliability needs of their systems. The project optimizes the Iroquois system to meet current and future gas supply needs of utility customers while minimizing environmental impact through compressor enhancements at existing compressor stations along the pipeline thereby avoiding land disturbances outside of existing facility footprints. The project&amp;#8217;s total capacity is approximately 125,000 Dth/day and it is 100% underpinned by 20-year term contracts. This project requires FERC and various federal and state permits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC) issued an order of public convenience and necessity for ExC on March 25, 2022.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On October 28, 2024, Iroquois requested FERC to issue an Order granting an extension of time until March 25, 2027, to complete the construction of the ExC Project and place the facilities into service. The FERC granted Iroquois&amp;#8217; request by Order dated February 19, 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On February 7, 2025, the Partnership received the necessary state air permits from the New York State Department of Environmental Conservation for each of the Athens and Dover Compressor Stations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;In Connecticut, on July 29, 2025, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Connecticut Department of Energy and Environmental Protection (CT DEEP) published a Notice of Tentative Determination (NTD) to Approve Point Source New Source Review Permit Applications.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The public comment period closed on September 16, 2025. A public informational hearing was held on January 8, 2026, with an additional comment period open until January 15, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;CT DEEP submitted its response to the public comments to the Hearing Office on July 24, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Also on July 24, 2026, the CT DEEP issued revised New Source Review (NSR) Permits and a NTD to Approve Point Source New Source Review Permit Applications, as amended.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The 30-day comment period closed on August 26, 2026. Iroquois submitted comments on the NTD and NSR permits, as amended. Requests for an adjudicatory hearing were submitted by opposition groups to the CT DEEP for consideration. Iroquois is preparing responses to those requests.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On August 14, 2026, Iroquois filed with the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC) a Request for a Limited Notice to Proceed to commence construction of approved gas cooling facilities and VRS at the Milford Compressor Station in Connecticut and all applicable ExC Project Facilities at the Athens and Dover Compressor Station in New York. The matter is pending before FERC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The project is projected to be placed in service in calendar year 2028. The estimated project cost including AFUDC is $380 million and upon receipt of all outstanding permits shall be revised in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;accordance with the terms and conditions set forth in precedent agreements executed with the project shippers. As of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;June 30, 2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, the Partnership has incurred approximately $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;36.7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; million of engineering and permitting related capital expenditures, including AFUDC. The Company currently believes it will obtain all necessary approvals for the project. However, in the event such permits are not granted, the Partnership expects to recover 50% of the expenditures incurred &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;up to $40 million based&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; upon agreements with third parties.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Property Tax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt; Proceedings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 1pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 13.7pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Nassau Country Property Tax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt; Settlement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;In January 2023, 2024, and 2025, Iroquois received and paid under protest tax bills representing the State of New York, Nassau County Tax Collection imposing real property taxes or special ad valorem levies upon Iroquois Property for the Nassau County Sewer Collection and Disposal District.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Iroquois pipeline is not located within the boundaries of the Nassau County Sewer District.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Iroquois filed complaints in April 2023, and 2024 challenging the sewer collection and disposal charges.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;By Settlement Agreement dated March 20, 2025, The State of New York, Nassau County agreed to reimburse Iroquois approximately $0.6 million as full settlement of all improperly imposed taxes assessed and billed on Iroquois Property as part of the Nassau County Sewer and Disposal District&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;for the tax years 2023, 2024 and 2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The State of New York Nassau County also agreed not to include the Iroquois Property in the District commencing with the 2026 county/town tax bills.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Iroquois received payment in full from the State of New York in June 2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; has recorded the benefit as a reduction of Taxes Other Than Income on the consolidated Statements of Comprehensive Income&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 13.7pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Bronx Property Tax &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Proceedings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On March 1, 2024, the&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Partnership&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; filed an &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;administrative &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;appeal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; and a judicial petition on October 16, 2024,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; of the tax assessment of a portion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; its Bronx facilities (known as the Eastchester Extension) with the Tax Commission of the City of New York (NYC Tax Commission)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; for the tax period ending June 30, 2025. On October 15, 2025, a petition was filed appealing the tax assessment for the tax period ending June 30, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The two matters were consolidated, and a hearing was held on both matters on September 30, 2025 (Consolidated Tax Appeals).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On February 12, 2026, the NYC Tax Commission proposed, and Iroquois accepted an &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;assessed property value of $3,000,000 for both years resulting in a settlement of the Consolidated Tax Appeals.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;To date, the Partnership has received $1.1 million of $1.6 million total anticipated settlement. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Litigation Proceedings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Partnership is a party to various legal matters incidental to its business. However, the Partnership believes that the outcome to these proceedings will not have a material adverse effect on the Partnership&amp;#8217;s financial condition or results of operations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 2pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;No liabilities have been recorded by the Partnership in conjunction with any legal matters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 150%; font-size: 3pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt; font-size: 8pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
